--
--   Description
-- 
-- 
-- This tests that the GEM operates correctly when in full duplex 
-- operation in gigabit mode.
-- 
-- Functional coverage
----------------------
-- � Ensures that the GEM does not defer to carrier sense in full duplex 
--     operation for gigabit mode.
-- � Ensures that collisions do not occur in full duplex operation for 
--     gigabit mode.
-- � Ensures that the GEM does not add extension to valid frames between 
--     64 bytes and 512 bytes long in full duplex operation for gigabit mode.
-- � Ensures that the GEM does not operate in burst gigabit mode in 
--     full-duplex operation.
-- � Ensures that the GEM does not include carrier extension in slot 
--     length checking.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for full-duplex gigabit operation.
-- 2. Set crs high for the whole test. (should have no affect 
--     in full-duplex mode)
-- 3. Transmit and receive a minimum sized frame at the same 
--     time. (GEM should not defer to carrier sense. Also, transmitted 
--     frame should have no extension added to it.)
-- 4. Transmit a minimum sized frame and create collisions during the 
--     frame transmission. (This should have no effect on the GEM.)
-- 5. Transmit a 200-byte frame and then a 511-byte frame. (There should 
--     be no extension added to the frames when they are transmitted.)
-- 6. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension. (This should not 
--     affect frame length statistics.)
-- 7. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure the above 
--     operations were handled properly.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

-- 1. Initialise the GEM for full-duplex gigabit operation.

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100)  00 00000000 -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr       00 0000000c -- enable transmit and receive
apbrd       24 00000000 -- check interrupt status
apbwr       28 ffffffff -- enable all interrupts
apbrd       24 00000000 -- check interrupt status
apbrd       30 00000000 -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbrd       04 00080000 -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd       08 00000006 -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr       04 0008040b -- indicate 1G operation, jumbo frames enabled
                        --  full duplex operation
apbrd       04 0008040b -- verify write to speed register..
apbwr       88 e3cc6388 -- address match 1 bottom
apbwr       8c 000015cc -- address match 1 top
apbrdf      20 00000000 -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame


-- 2. Set crs high for the whole test. (should have no affect 
--     in full-duplex mode)
pinsd(100) crs 1

